{
  "kanji": "市",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 市\ntitle: city; market\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 巾\nradicalNumber: 50\nonyomi: [シ]\nkunyomi: [いち]\ndistractors: [席, 常, 師]\n---\n\n# 市 — city; market\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 巾 (no. 50) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n市 connects two useful areas of vocabulary: cities and markets.\n[市民](../words/市民.md) しみん names citizens or city residents, and 市役所 しやくしょ is a city hall.\nThe kun reading appears in 市場 いちば, a marketplace.\nDo not assume that every word containing 市 means a market.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture a small canopy above the hanging 巾 shape, like a stall you pass in a city.\nThis is a memory image based on the written shape, not a historical claim.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| シ | on | [市民](../words/市民.md) しみん — citizens; 市役所 しやくしょ — city hall |\n| いち | kun | 市場 いちば — marketplace |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [市民](../words/市民.md) しみん — citizen; city resident\n- 市役所 しやくしょ — city hall; municipal office\n- 市場 いちば — marketplace\n\n## Notes\n\n市 is indexed under 巾, visible in its lower part.\n[席](席.md), [常](常.md), and [師](師.md) also contain 巾, but have more material above or beside it.\nThe dictionary has more than one sense of 市民; its civic meaning is not limited to a literal market community.\n\nSources: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project);\n[JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1308690, 1308760, 1308300.\n",
